1
00:00:00,710 --> 00:00:03,420
HAPPY GRADUATION!
Kyoka, congrats on graduating!

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,960
Congrats!

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:08,210
Thank you so much, everyone.

4
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:10,710
When do you get to turn human?

5
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:12,710
In two days' time.

6
00:00:12,790 --> 00:00:15,210
With the scholarship I received
from the director,

7
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:18,290
I'll be moving next to the dance school.

8
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:19,330
Huh?

9
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:21,500
Kyoka, is that...

10
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:26,130
It's a commemorative gift
for graduating students.

11
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,880
Even after I become human
and lose my memories of this place,

12
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:36,460
wearing this ring will let me remember
it all and enter the school barrier.

13
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:40,580
Mr. Hitoma.

14
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,380
Thank you for everything
over the past year.

15
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:46,500
You've worked hard, Minazuki.

16
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:52,960
When you told me about your
shortcomings, it was a revelation.

17
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:56,330
I had longed to be perfect,
but being imperfect is fine.

18
00:00:56,960 --> 00:01:02,960
And helping each other to overcome those
imperfections is what makes one human.

19
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:05,000
Yeah, that's right.

20
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:06,830
Mr. Hitoma.

21
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:12,420
Thank you for teaching me
what it is to be human.

22
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:13,420
Minazuki.

23
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:17,210
Thanks for letting me be your teacher.

24
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:53,380
EPISODE 7: THE MISANTHROPE AND THE FRUITLESS LOVE FORTUNE
That marks the end of another school year!

25
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,330
EPISODE 7: THE MISANTHROPE AND THE FRUITLESS LOVE FORTUNE
Cheers, everyone!

26
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:57,750
Cheers!

27
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:00,130
Oh, you're too kind.

28
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:03,080
I haven't had drinks
with co-workers in so long.

29
00:03:03,170 --> 00:03:04,670
Mr. Hitoma.

30
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,540
Your cup's looking empty.

31
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:09,130
Oh, thank you.

32
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:11,040
Have some, too, Ms. Saotome.

33
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:14,750
Oh, I prefer this.

34
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:16,540
Sake?

35
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,170
Ms. Yuki, control yourself.

36
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:20,380
How many bottles have you had?

37
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,380
Um...

38
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:25,750
You sure do drink like a fish.

39
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,540
Didn't you promise to hold back
when we're in public?

40
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:32,210
We only get to celebrate
like this once a year!

41
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:33,710
Stop making excuses.

42
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,710
Just look at the shock
on Mr. Hitoma's face.

43
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,040
What?
You've got the wrong idea!

44
00:03:38,130 --> 00:03:41,420
I used to be a yuki-onna
who lived in a cold region,

45
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,170
which is why I can hold my liquor!

46
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:45,830
What? You used to be a yuki-onna?!

47
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:48,130
Did I never mention it?

48
00:03:48,210 --> 00:03:50,210
Were you aware of this, Mr. Hoshino?

49
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:51,830
Well, yes.

50
00:03:52,670 --> 00:03:56,290
Mr. Hoshino, were you a non-human as well?

51
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:59,080
No, I've always been human.

52
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:04,380
That reminds me, I was drinking
when we first met, Mr. Hoshino.

53
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:07,420
When I got stranded up
on a snowy mountain.

54
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:12,960
I saw a woman in a kimono holding a
sake bottle and thought I was a goner.

55
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,830
How mean!

56
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,960
That brings back memories, though.

57
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,960
The moment I fell in love at first sight.

58
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:21,130
What?

59
00:04:21,210 --> 00:04:25,210
I didn't expect you to follow me all
the way to America after that.

60
00:04:25,290 --> 00:04:27,330
Huh? Hey, um...

61
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:29,790
Would the two of you happen to be...

62
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,330
We're married.

63
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,290
Husband and wife?!

64
00:04:34,630 --> 00:04:40,580
<i>So that handkerchief I stained was a gift</i>
<i>from Ms. Saotome to Mr. Hoshino?</i>

65
00:04:40,670 --> 00:04:42,920
<i>Oh, it all makes sense now...</i>

66
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:51,920
Finally, my own place
in the staff dormitory!

67
00:04:52,670 --> 00:04:56,210
An apartment with an eight-tatami bedroom
and twelve-tatami living-dining space!

68
00:04:56,290 --> 00:05:00,170
And all for the stellar rent of 20,000
yen per month, utilities included!

69
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,080
A corner room on the top floor.

70
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:05,630
And no one's moved in below or next door,
so I can be loud as I want!

71
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:07,920
It's a paradise for a gamer like me!

72
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,460
I'm here to visit.

73
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:15,250
How'd you know I moved in?

74
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:18,170
Mr. Hitoma, thanks for your
hard work over the past year.

75
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:19,880
Why are you here?

76
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:23,960
I bet it was pretty different
from your last school.

77
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,250
What'd you think?

78
00:05:25,330 --> 00:05:28,330
What kind of question is that?
Are you supposed to be my co-worker?

79
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:29,880
Well, how was it?

80
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,750
Think you'll still stay on?

81
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,250
Let me think.

82
00:05:34,630 --> 00:05:38,170
A lot happened,
but I had a decent time.

83
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:40,830
I see. Good to hear it.

84
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,880
Oh, and the principal wants to see you.

85
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,670
What?! Tell me that <i>first</i>!

86
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:50,960
There's someone I'd like you to meet.

87
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:55,330
None other than the director
of Shiranui High School.

88
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:57,380
The director?

89
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,710
She's waiting in the director's office.

90
00:05:59,790 --> 00:06:02,420
Come with me, and I'll introduce you.

91
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:04,210
U-Understood.

92
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,500
Pardon us.

93
00:06:10,210 --> 00:06:11,330
We're here.

94
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,000
Haneda?

95
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,290
It's a pleasure to meet you, Mr. Hitoma.

96
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:23,630
I was happy to hear your time
at this school has been decent.

97
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,380
Let me formally introduce you.

98
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:42,460
This is our director, Lady Shiranui.

99
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:45,380
She happens to be a phoenix.

100
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:49,670
The most powerful being,
who reigns over all of existence.

101
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:51,670
A phoenix?

102
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:54,790
And I am a crow tengu.

103
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:55,750
What?

104
00:06:56,380 --> 00:07:00,920
I can see a month into the future,
albeit in fragments.

105
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,210
Thus, I knew you would
do well at this school,

106
00:07:05,290 --> 00:07:08,130
which is why I decided to hire you.

107
00:07:08,210 --> 00:07:09,830
See into the future?

108
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,750
Sorry to take you by surprise.

109
00:07:11,830 --> 00:07:15,830
Tobari Haneda is a form I take
to observe the students more intimately.

110
00:07:16,290 --> 00:07:18,580
Um, D-Director?

111
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:23,040
How should I be treating
you going forward?

112
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:25,420
The way you always have, if you would.

113
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:30,040
As a precaution, let me warn you
that I'll fire you if you reveal who I am.

114
00:07:30,130 --> 00:07:32,500
The same goes for whoever finds out.

115
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:36,580
May I ask who else knows about this?

116
00:07:36,670 --> 00:07:40,290
Just me and Haruka, the school nurse.

117
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,580
That reminds me.

118
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:46,500
Last fall, you were worried
when I had fallen ill.

119
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:48,130
Thanks for your concern back then.

120
00:07:48,210 --> 00:07:51,040
Oh, I'd forgotten all about that.

121
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:55,330
I always exhaust myself every year
preparing for the new students.

122
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,580
So that's what it was.

123
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,290
When I first established this school,
it was nothing more than on a whim.

124
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:05,080
But over time, I began to enjoy it.

125
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:11,630
I love seeing mortal
beings try their best.

126
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:14,920
That's why I decided to enroll
as a student to become human.

127
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:21,080
My goal is to turn human so
I can draw my last breath.

128
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:29,080
Watching them made me want to live
for the sake of facing death.

129
00:08:29,170 --> 00:08:30,330
I see...

130
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:35,130
Hey, Mr. Hitoma. Do you like humans?

131
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:44,580
Humans are selfish and
don't care about others.

132
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:49,000
Good people are taken advantage
of, and honesty gets you nowhere.

133
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,460
I hate humans.

134
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:59,290
I may hate humans, but I think
I'm fine with that for now.

135
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Sure.

136
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:05,960
Here's to a new school year.

137
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,710
ADVANCED CLASS
<i>Okay, first day of the new term.</i>

138
00:09:11,330 --> 00:09:13,880
<i>Last year, it was a Soran Bushi dance...</i>

139
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:21,710
I love you!

140
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,670
Mr. Rei! Please marry me!

141
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,130
What?!

142
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:28,960
Hmph!

143
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,750
What's the big idea, Sui?

144
00:09:30,830 --> 00:09:32,830
Karin, stop destroying
the moral fiber of our classroom!

145
00:09:33,210 --> 00:09:36,130
And Hitoma, you're a teacher,
so stop blushing!

146
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:39,170
I'm in the middle of talking
to the teacher.

147
00:09:39,250 --> 00:09:40,960
Could you please pipe down, Sui?

148
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:41,920
What?!

149
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:45,630
What a riot.

150
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:50,080
Mr. Hitoma, aren't you going to
respond to Karin's proposal?

151
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:52,330
Huh? Um...

152
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:55,040
I want two kids!

153
00:09:55,130 --> 00:09:56,460
Where'd <i>that</i> come from?!

154
00:09:57,250 --> 00:09:58,710
Ah, well...

155
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:01,790
Sorry, but I can't marry you.

156
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:02,830
Why not?!

157
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,830
Huh? What kind of...

158
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:06,250
I mean, first off.

159
00:10:06,710 --> 00:10:08,380
You're just messing with me, aren't you?

160
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:10,330
Not at all!

161
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:12,960
I really love you, Mr. Rei!

162
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,210
What?

163
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:17,330
Mr. Rei, please believe me.

164
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:21,750
<i>No, I won't be led astray.</i>

165
00:10:22,170 --> 00:10:24,790
<i>I know! I'll recite all</i>
<i>of the Japanese eras.</i>

166
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:27,830
<i>Taika, Hakuchi, Shucho, Taiho, Keiun, Wado</i>

167
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:31,420
Mr. Rei? Mr. Rei!

168
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,250
<i>– Tenpyo-shoho, Tenpyo-hoji...</i>
– He's frozen up.

169
00:10:33,790 --> 00:10:37,920
Okay. Let's move on to our first
homeroom of the new school year.

170
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,830
First, let's introduce ourselves...

171
00:10:45,710 --> 00:10:47,460
Kurosawa, wake up.

172
00:10:50,790 --> 00:10:52,040
Who're you?

173
00:10:52,130 --> 00:10:55,250
The advanced class homeroom
teacher, Rei Hitoma.

174
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:56,670
I see...

175
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:57,790
Hey, wake up!

176
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:02,130
Oh, are you feeling unwell?

177
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:03,460
I'm fine.

178
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,080
That's good...

179
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:09,330
In that case, hang in there
just a little longer.

180
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:12,040
We'll be done after a short talk.

181
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:13,920
Let's continue our introductions.

182
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:18,130
My name is Rei Hitoma.
I teach social studies.

183
00:11:18,210 --> 00:11:21,460
This is my second year being
in charge of the advanced class.

184
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:23,880
I hope we can have a great year together.

185
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:24,830
Thanks.

186
00:11:25,750 --> 00:11:26,750
Now for...

187
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:29,330
Let me introduce myself first!

188
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:32,790
I'm Karin Ryuzaki, and I just moved up
to the advanced class.

189
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,080
I belong to the noble dragon family.

190
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:38,290
I want to become human to find love.

191
00:11:38,710 --> 00:11:43,460
So Mr. Rei, will you teach me about love?

192
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:44,830
Not happening.

193
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,170
Grr...

194
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:49,210
I haven't set off
the right event flag yet?

195
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:51,880
I will not give up!

196
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:55,500
I'll <i>ensure</i> that you fall in love
and agree to marry me!

197
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:56,880
Just you wait!

198
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:59,380
Okay, you're up next, Nezu.

199
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:00,710
You got it!

200
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:03,830
I'm Machi! Machi Nezu!
I'm a mouse!

201
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:08,630
I want to become human so
I can eat lots of tasty food!

202
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:10,880
What a simple-minded reason.

203
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:15,920
Something tasty I ate lately is
our dorm mom Ryouko's homemade pudding!

204
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,790
The trend nowadays is silky-soft pudding,

205
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:23,080
but Ryouko's is on the firmer side
with a rich, milky flavor,

206
00:12:23,170 --> 00:12:26,380
not to mention how you
can really taste the eggs!

207
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:28,790
Sounds more like a food review
than an introduction.

208
00:12:29,710 --> 00:12:31,130
Next, Kurosawa.

209
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,960
Neneko Kurosawa. Cat.

210
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:38,880
My reason for wanting
to become human... is a secret.

211
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:46,040
Neneko wouldn't tell the intermediate
class last year why she wants to be human.

212
00:12:46,130 --> 00:12:47,500
I never knew that.

213
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:50,040
Neneko's always been like that.

214
00:12:50,130 --> 00:12:52,630
Putting on an act
because she thinks it's cool—

215
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:57,420
Huh? What is it?

216
00:13:00,290 --> 00:13:01,790
What do you want?

217
00:13:04,460 --> 00:13:07,250
S-Say something!

218
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:10,420
I—

219
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:13,830
So scary!

220
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:16,580
Help me, Mr. Hitoma!

221
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:17,670
She's so scary!

222
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:19,580
I didn't say anything yet.

223
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,670
You were flashing your fangs at me!

224
00:13:22,750 --> 00:13:25,920
You definitely want to gobble me up!

225
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,580
You're paranoid.

226
00:13:28,290 --> 00:13:30,580
And I bet you taste bad, Machi.

227
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:33,420
That ticks me off in its own way!

228
00:13:34,130 --> 00:13:35,080
Good morning.

229
00:13:35,170 --> 00:13:36,040
Good morning!

230
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:43,540
Mr. Rei! I love you!

231
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,790
You're supposed to greet
people with "good morning."

232
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:48,330
By the way, wanna marry me?

233
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:49,750
Not really.

234
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:51,170
Boo...

235
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:52,710
Take this!

236
00:13:54,830 --> 00:13:58,460
<i>Th-Th-This feeling on my back...</i>

237
00:13:58,830 --> 00:14:01,830
What's up, Mr. Hitoma? You look so funny!

238
00:14:02,630 --> 00:14:05,210
Ohgami. Help me.

239
00:14:05,290 --> 00:14:08,330
I get it. You're killing me here!

240
00:14:08,790 --> 00:14:11,380
Karin-rin, are you down bad
for Mr. Hitoma?

241
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:12,710
Like, <i>serious</i> serious?

242
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:16,670
Or do you just think it's funny to toy
with him like Isaki?

243
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:19,710
I'm downright serious.

244
00:14:19,790 --> 00:14:21,710
Omigosh, that's adorbs!

245
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:24,460
Karin-rin's, like, <i>so</i> cute!

246
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:26,460
Loving it. You go, girl!

247
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:30,960
It's the first time I've seen you
like this, but you're pretty funny.

248
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,960
For real? Thanks!

249
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:36,330
Hope you vibe with both Isaki and Isaki!

250
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:39,250
Can you get off me already?

251
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:44,000
See you all tomorrow.

252
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:49,830
Hey Karin-rin, tell me more about
that natural makeup from before!

253
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:52,880
You mean the cosmetics from ancient times?
Sure thing.

254
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:55,580
Oh, I need to talk to you, Ryuzaki.

255
00:14:55,670 --> 00:14:57,750
Can you spare a moment right now?

256
00:14:58,170 --> 00:15:01,250
What?!
You want to confess your love, Mr. Rei?!

257
00:15:01,330 --> 00:15:02,960
You know that's not it.

258
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:05,790
Karin-rin, I'll be waiting for you.

259
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:06,750
Sure!

260
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:14,460
– Ryuzaki.
– Y-Yes?

261
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:17,080
About this morning.

262
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:20,460
You shouldn't be so clingy with me,
so let's not do that.

263
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:26,960
Also, I don't know how serious you are,
but I can't go along with it,

264
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:30,540
so I'd like you to stop
with the sudden declarations of love.

265
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:35,790
You see why, right? So please.

266
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,130
I don't wanna.

267
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:41,250
I don't wanna, I don't wanna!
I don't wanna, I don't wanna!

268
00:15:41,330 --> 00:15:44,630
I won't stop telling you
that I love you, Mr. Rei!

269
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:47,080
Huh? But why?

270
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:51,040
Since I'm in love with you, of course!

271
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:56,170
Why me, of all people?

272
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:57,670
Well...

273
00:15:58,710 --> 00:16:02,670
Mr. Rei, remember when you
snuck off campus with Sui?

274
00:16:02,750 --> 00:16:03,630
What?!

275
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:08,250
I was tailing Sui that day.

276
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:10,790
That's when I saw you, Mr. Rei.

277
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:16,790
Back then, you were absolutely stunning.

278
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:24,040
Despite looking hesitant,
you chose to leave school with Sui, right?

279
00:16:27,330 --> 00:16:30,830
I want to become human to find love.

280
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:34,540
I want to find love
to be cherished by someone.

281
00:16:35,130 --> 00:16:39,250
Seeing you take action for your student,
all while hesitating,

282
00:16:39,330 --> 00:16:40,920
I couldn't help but fall in love.

283
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,500
Isn't it lame to be so hesitant?

284
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:50,170
Your reservations show
that you gave it some thought.

285
00:16:50,830 --> 00:16:53,130
I can't think of anything cooler.

286
00:16:53,540 --> 00:16:56,170
Really laying it on there, huh?

287
00:16:57,040 --> 00:17:01,920
Mr. Rei, you're a wonderful
human who cherishes others.

288
00:17:03,630 --> 00:17:05,130
Long ago...

289
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,880
I knew a human just like that.

290
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:15,250
It was an era when I could
still live close to humans.

291
00:17:15,330 --> 00:17:17,580
I inhabited a cave in the mountains,

292
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:21,330
spending my days warding off the humans
and animals that'd wander in.

293
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:24,670
I may have been alone,
but I led a comfortable life.

294
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:30,290
Until one day, an injured human
princess appeared before me.

295
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:34,460
The princess cherished me so.

296
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:38,330
I learned from her
how nice it feels to be petted.

297
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:42,790
To this day, I still remember
our final day together.

298
00:17:44,170 --> 00:17:46,630
A prince from a neighboring
kingdom showed up.

299
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:51,290
He was under the impression that I had
kidnapped the princess to hold captive.

300
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:56,750
And so he brought a large
number of soldiers to my cave.

301
00:17:57,790 --> 00:18:00,710
Since they took up swords against me,
I had no choice but to fight,

302
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:04,290
but human attacks
were completely ineffective on me.

303
00:18:04,830 --> 00:18:07,960
When I was about
to wipe out the prince's army,

304
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:10,540
the princess began to plead with me.

305
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:14,080
"Please don't hurt the poor
prince any longer," she said.

306
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:19,040
The princess left with the prince
to return to human society...

307
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:21,790
Paying no mind to what would become of me.

308
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:25,040
It was then that I first felt it.

309
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:27,580
I was jealous of the prince.

310
00:18:27,670 --> 00:18:32,460
Cherished by the princess,
protected by her, in her embrace.

311
00:18:33,290 --> 00:18:38,880
Had I been weak like him,
would the princess have stayed by my side?

312
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:45,790
I was unmatched in my strength,
which is why no one thought to cherish me.

313
00:18:47,630 --> 00:18:51,460
The ages passed, and humans
spread across the globe.

314
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:57,250
So that I would not harm them,
I began living where no humans approached.

315
00:18:58,250 --> 00:18:59,830
That's when I first heard it.

316
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:05,670
Rumors of the keeper of the sea's daughter
who went off to a school to become human.

317
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:07,880
You mean Minazuki?

318
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,290
I knew then that I'd found it.

319
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:14,750
By becoming human, I could
stand on equal footing with them.

320
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:16,380
To stay by their side forever.

321
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:18,170
To be cherished by them!

322
00:19:18,710 --> 00:19:21,710
I yearned for their affection.

323
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:26,250
I want to become human
and live a life where I fall in love.

324
00:19:27,130 --> 00:19:30,880
You treat people honestly,
even those who aren't human.

325
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:33,880
You listen to what we
have to say as equals.

326
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:38,790
That's why I love you,
and want to be loved by you.

327
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,750
It has to be you, Mr. Rei.

328
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:46,330
Ryuzaki.

329
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:52,790
Sorry. It still stands
that I'm your teacher.

330
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:56,290
You can't make advances on a student?

331
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,540
That's part of it.

332
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:03,420
I care for you and the rest of my students
solely as a teacher.

333
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:09,790
So it wouldn't be right to treat one of
you as special by, say, falling in love.

334
00:20:11,330 --> 00:20:14,580
If you're going to push me away,
then at least be firm about it.

335
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:16,290
Sorry.

336
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:20,580
I understand. I'm sorry for bothering you.

337
00:20:22,670 --> 00:20:26,790
It's fine. I'm used to being alone.

338
00:20:32,210 --> 00:20:33,080
Ryuzaki.

339
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:37,380
I won't fall in love with you.

340
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:42,040
But romantic feelings aren't
the only reason to stay by someone's side.

341
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:46,630
As your teacher, I don't
want to see you all alone.

342
00:20:47,170 --> 00:20:50,080
Until the day comes that you graduate.

343
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:53,790
You really don't play fair, Mr. Rei.

344
00:20:54,290 --> 00:20:57,960
That said, I still
can't help but love you.

345
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:02,960
So until I graduate
and leave this school as a human,

346
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:06,130
don't make me give up
on my love for you.

347
00:21:07,210 --> 00:21:11,830
You just said you don't want to
see me all alone, didn't you?

348
00:21:12,670 --> 00:21:13,580
Ryuzaki...

349
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,080
I don't need to hear your answer.

350
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:17,630
I'll see you tomorrow!

351
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:19,460
Hey, wait!

352
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:29,670
He turned me down!

353
00:21:29,750 --> 00:21:32,170
Karin-rin, you did everything you could.

354
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:33,380
Good job.

355
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:35,460
We can talk it out all you like.

356
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,670
Yeah. Yeah!

357
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:45,170
Good morning!

358
00:21:46,790 --> 00:21:50,670
I should stop gaming until the last minute
just because the dorm's so close...

359
00:21:51,830 --> 00:21:54,380
Mr. Rei! Good morning!

360
00:21:54,460 --> 00:21:56,630
Oh, Ryuzaki. Morning.

361
00:21:58,170 --> 00:21:59,540
I love you today, too!

362
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:39,960
NEXT EPISODE: THE MISANTHROPE AND THE MAGIC FOR PEACE AND QUIET

